    "text": "<p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/32_solu_chem_par_2.jpg\"/></p><p>(i) I and II follow <math><msub><mrow><mi>S</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub><mn>2</mn></math>  mechanism as they are primary</p><p>(ii) Reactivity order IV > I > III</p><p>(iii) I and III follows <math><msub><mrow><mi>S</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub><mn>1</mn></math>  mechanism as they form stable carbocation</p><p>(iv) Compound IV undergoes inversion of configuration.</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/25113_1.jpg\"/></p>",
